# The IEC inner identifier module (issue #706 §4) — the inner IEC document
# face as a referenceable library, NOT the declared IEC scheme (tier D
# stays coded; the study draft data/iec/legacy-notation.md defines the
# inner faces this module carries).
#
# `EN IEC 60335-1:2020` adoptions bind this module so the adopted segment
# has a declared face and a declared identity.

module: iec.inner
version: 1
title: "The IEC inner identifier face"
description: >-
  The inner IEC document face an adoption names: the IEC publisher token,
  the document number with its part, and the year. The module carries the
  face, not the IEC scheme — the typed-stage surface and the consolidated
  wave stay with the coded flavor (tier D, out of PFS scope).

grammar:
  iec_space: '" "'
  iec_colon: '":"'
  iec_dash: '"-"'
  iec_year: '4*digit'
  iec_part: '1*digit'
  iec_number: '("6" 4*digit / 5*digit / 1*digit) [iec_dash iec_part]'
  iec_document: '"IEC" iec_space iec_number [iec_colon iec_year]'

tokens:
  - "IEC"

identity:
  composition: wrapper-with-adopted
  base_module: iec.inner
  adopted_field: adopted

hooks:
  inner_parse: >-
    The adopted segment's parse — the coded-hook escape hatch, as for
    iso.inner. An EN adoption of an IEC document parses this face.
